1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,930
Good afternoon, Dreamtime Travel. How can I help you?

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:08,770
Oh hello. I'm interested in the holidays you offer along the coast near here.

3
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:14,630
Yes. We operate several tours up the coast. Where in particular did you want to go?

4
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:20,550
Well, I like the sound of the holiday that mentioned whales. Was it 'Whale Watching'?

5
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:22,893
Oh, that's our Whale Watch Experience.

6
00:00:22,893 --> 00:00:28,360
It's very popular and it's based in a lovely little town with nice beaches.

7
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:31,140
Oh right, and how long does it last?

8
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:36,700
It's two days. That includes four hours' travel time each way from here.

9
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:42,200
Good, I don't want to be away any longer than that. So is that by coach?

10
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:46,122
Actually it's by minibus. We like to keep those tours small

11
00:00:46,122 --> 00:00:50,045
and personal so we don't take a whole coachload of people.

12
00:00:50,045 --> 00:00:54,520
In fact, we only take up to fifteen people on this tour

13
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,890
although we do run it with just twelve or thirteen.

14
00:00:57,890 --> 00:01:01,090
Oh, right. So do you run these tours often?

15
00:01:01,090 --> 00:01:03,534
Well it depends on the time of year.

16
00:01:03,534 --> 00:01:07,810
Of course in peak times like the summer holidays we do them every weekend,

17
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:11,170
but at the moment it's usually once a month at most.

18
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:13,110
And when is the next one going?

19
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:22,846
Mmm, let me see. Um, there's one in three weeks' time which is April the 18th,

20
00:01:22,846 --> 00:01:29,540
and then we don't have another one until June the 2nd.

21
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:33,640
All right, and is April a good time to go?

22
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:37,608
Pretty good. Though the really good time is later in the year.

23
00:01:37,608 --> 00:01:43,230
I have to say though that the whale sighting is only one of the many things offered.

24
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:44,000
Really?

25
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,950
Yes. The hotel itself where you stay has great facilities. It's called The Pallisades.

26
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:51,650
The Paris what?

27
00:01:51,650 --> 00:02:02,540
NO, it's actually The Pallisades, P-A-L-L-I-S-A-D-E-S. It's right on the main beach there.

28
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,530
Oh, I see.

29
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:08,170
All of the rooms have nice views and the food is really good there too.

30
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:11,140
Oh right.

31
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:15,780
And what about the other things? You know, that are included in the price.

32
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,853
Oh, there are lots of things.

33
00:02:17,853 --> 00:02:21,308
If you don't want to do the whale watch cruise,

34
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:27,874
your guide will take anyone who is interested either on a bushwalk through the national park near the hotel,

35
00:02:27,874 --> 00:02:32,020
and there's no extra charge for that, or on a fishing trip.

36
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,093
That's an extra $12 I think.

37
00:02:34,093 --> 00:02:38,930
And there's also a reptile park in town. That costs more or less the same.

38
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:41,680
No, I think I'd prefer whales to snakes.

39
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:48,500
Yeah. And if you just want to relax you are free to sit by the hotel pool or go down the beach.

40
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:51,820
Oh, and they also have tennis courts at the hotel

41
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:54,700
but you have to pay for those by the hour.

42
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,880
But there are table tennis tables downstairs

43
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,040
and they're part of the accommodation package.

44
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,590
Just speak to your guide.

45
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:05,060
Well that sounds good. So how much is the basic tour price?

46
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:09,320
At this time of year it's usually around $300

47
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:15,930
but let me check. Er... oh, it's actually $280.

48
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:19,070
And the next tour, are there any places on that one?

49
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,210
How many people is it for?

50
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,360
There are two of us.

51
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:24,270
Yes, that should be fine.

52
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:33,440
Can I just mention that we require all bookings to be made at least fourteen days before you travel to avoid cancellations of tours.

53
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:37,460
And if you cancel within seven days of departure

54
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,700
you will have to pay 50% of your total booking.

55
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:41,630
OK.

56
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:46,670
And you also need to pay a 20% deposit at the time of booking.

57
00:03:46,670 --> 00:03:48,670
Can I pay that by credit card?

58
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:49,930
Yes, you can.

59
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:53,880
All right, what I'll do is I'll talk to my partner and get back to you.

60
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:58,580
Fine. So I'll make a provisional booking, shall I

61
00:03:59,180 --> 00:03:59,465
Two for the Whale Watch Experience.

62
00:03:59,465 --> 00:04:05,280
Let me issue you with a customer reference number for when you call back

63
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,540
Do you have a pen?

64
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:07,280
Yes.

65
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:11,385
OK, it's three nine seven, four five, T.

66
00:04:11,385 --> 00:04:17,260
That's T for tango. When you call back

67
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:20,620
ask to speak to the Tour Manager, that's me, Tracy.

68
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:22,130
Fine, I will.
